<title>USA: Continental starts Honolulu maintenance unit.</title>
<headline>Continental starts Honolulu maintenance unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines said construction work has started on its $24 million, 112,000 sq ft maintenance facility at Honolulu.</p>
<p>The carrier officially announced the plans for the facility on April 11.</p>
<p>The facility, due to be completed in spring 1998, will be used for maintenance on Continental's fleet of Boeing 747s and DC-10s, a company spokeswoman said. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
